# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion SHIP gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-ship-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the approved commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-octo3-ship-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# GX1 (STOP): EXACTNESS of the ship profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-o3 against its control GX0 on the same image: the same prompts,
# unaudited. READ: python3 scripts/ci/parked_compare.py --control <GX0 smoke log> --parked <GX1 smoke log> --control-container <GX0 container log> --parked-container <GX1
# container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-o3: every levern_equal, levern_equal_busy and parked_equal content hash EQUAL (the last
# w2-er GX: 37 of 37), compared above 0, the parked judge with 0 problems under the lever band. Any difference is NO-GO for shipping. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter holding it, power, current,
# temperature, kernel NOPs); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs on the host and
# reads only. OCTO READ (tp4/octo-3, the shape and its three levers run under this profile's waiver): python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container log>
# --profile <ship profile> clean, i.e. exactly one '[OCTO] admitted mode=live ... (owner traffic waiver <id>)' line; the six '[OCTO] UNQUALIFIED' lines, which are EXPECTED
# here (they are the card questions the waiver stands in for: the 'no UNQUALIFIED admission line' of an SR read applies to the 262k evidence waiver, not to them); at least
# 16 rounds with shape=octo at 8 live and rows=8 and no program compiled on the first octo round; the octo draft engaged once and serving at least half of the octo rounds
# at 8 live with no fallback or disabled line; the bundled attention engaged once with its call line; the glue8 engaged lines at users=8 rows=8 for every site and no
# fell-back line; the K/V page writer's 'octo 8-row served path' line once; the TAP window lever's engaged line and no fell-back line. concurrent8_steady is the test that
# supplies the octo rounds (the skew, stall and drain shapes run below six live seats most of the time). Duration (estimate): 15 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-ship-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-o3
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,parked_equal,parked_budgets,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=exactness ship arm: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
C2_TELEMETRY=1
